                <pb facs="1098" n="1002" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg1002"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.0667/8</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crosby</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received September 3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2035</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: … Referring to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 44 of June 25 regarding the exemption of Diplomatic and Consular officers
                    from the payment of consumption taxes, I have the honor to report that the
                    Foreign Office has recommended favorably to the Council of Ministers the action
                    requested by the Diplomatic Corps. As late as August 9th the Foreign Office had
                    received no reply to its recommendations.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon Leavitt
                    Crosby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
